    "long_instructions": "Luka’s finally ready to open his laundromat in Regreston. Regreston has a population of 5,000 and two existing laundromats. Luka will keep his laundromat open 24 hours, and it will be for residential use.\r\n\r\nHow many machines does your model predict Luka should buy?\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRemember you can get a prediction with `model.predict`, then print that prediction.\r\n\r\n```\r\nprediction = model.predict(...)\r\nprint(prediction)\r\n```\r\n\r\nConsider the argument you’ll pass to `model.predict` to match Bob’s description. It must be a list of encoded feature values inside a list itself. For example:\r\n\r\n```\r\nprediction = model.predict([[5, 2, 1, 0, 0, 1]])\r\n```\r\n\r\nOrder your feature value in the same order as the columns of your feature matrix. Remember that `OneHotEncoder` creates columns alphabetically.",
